---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Cycle Easy - Support"
  description="Get help with Cycle Easy, the privacy-first period tracker. FAQ and contact information."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/cycle-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Cycle Easy?</p>
          <p>Check the FAQ below, or email us at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Cycle%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <div class="faq-section">
            <h3 class="faq-category">Privacy & Security</h3>
            
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Is my period data really private?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Yes, absolutely. Cycle Easy stores all data locally on your device only. There are no servers, no cloud storage, no accounts, and no way for anyone — including us — to access your information. We built the app this way intentionally because we believe menstrual health data deserves the strongest possible privacy protections.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Can my data be subpoenaed or requested by law enforcement?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>We cannot produce data we don't have. Cycle Easy has no servers, no databases, and no user records. Your data exists only on your device. We literally cannot comply with data requests because we possess nothing to hand over. Your data is protected by your device's security and any legal protections that apply to your personal property.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">What does Cycle Easy share with Apple Health?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Only menstrual flow, and only if you connect Apple Health (during setup or in Settings → Apple Health). Cycle Easy reads menstrual flow, so periods saved in Apple Health or another app show up in your calendar, and writes menstrual flow for each day of the periods you log. Symptoms, notes and predictions stay in Cycle Easy. Health data stays in Apple Health on your iPhone, and we never see it. To stop, tap Stop syncing in Settings → Apple Health; to remove access, open the Health app, tap your profile, then Apps, then Cycle Easy.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Does the app collect any analytics?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>No. Cycle Easy contains zero analytics, crash reporting, advertising, or third-party SDKs. We don't track how you use the app, which features are popular, or even how many people have downloaded it. We accept this trade-off because your privacy matters more than our metrics.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-section">
            <h3 class="faq-category">Using the App</h3>
            
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">How do I log my period?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>On Today, tap Start period when your period starts, pick the flow (spotting, light, medium or heavy) and tap Add. When it ends, tap End period today. To log a past period, open the calendar, tap the day it started, then tap Period started this day.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">How accurate are the predictions?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Cycle Easy expects your next period one average cycle after your last one started, using your last six cycles. Until you've logged two periods, it uses the usual cycle length you set in Settings. Cycles naturally vary, so predictions are estimates, not certainties, and they aren't medical advice.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">What symptoms can I track?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Body symptoms like cramps, headaches, backache, bloating and tender breasts; moods like calm, anxious or irritable; and others like cravings, trouble sleeping and hot flashes. Insights shows which cycle days each one usually comes on. Symptom data stays on your device like everything else.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">What about fertility tracking?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Cycle Easy can show an estimated fertile window, but it's off by default; turn it on in Settings → Cycle. <strong>Important:</strong> it's an estimate for awareness only and must not be used for contraception or to plan a pregnancy. Talk to a healthcare provider about family planning.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-section">
            <h3 class="faq-category">Data Management</h3>
            
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">How do I export my data?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Open the menu, tap Settings, then Export data. You get a JSON file with your periods and symptoms to save or share however you like. Import data, in the same place, reads it back.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">How do I delete all my data?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Open Settings and tap Delete all data. This permanently erases every period and symptom from your device (and, if Apple Health is connected, the periods Cycle Easy saved there). Uninstalling the app also deletes everything. Since there's no cloud copy, deletion is permanent.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Can I transfer data to a new phone?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Yes, with a file you control. Cycle Easy keeps its data out of iCloud and computer backups, so export your data on the old iPhone (Settings → Export data), move the file to the new one (AirDrop works well), and tap Settings → Import data there. If you connected Apple Health, your periods are also in Apple Health, and Cycle Easy reads them back once you connect it on the new iPhone.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">What happens if I lose my phone?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Your Cycle Easy data is protected by your device's passcode and encryption, and you can add App lock (Settings → App lock) so Face ID, Touch ID or your passcode is needed to open the app. If your phone is lost and you don't have an export, the data is gone, which from a privacy point of view can be a feature rather than a bug.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-section">
            <h3 class="faq-category">General</h3>
            
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Is Cycle Easy free?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Yes, Cycle Easy is completely free with no subscriptions, no in-app purchases, and no ads. We believe privacy-first period tracking should be accessible to everyone.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Why don't you offer cloud backup?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Cloud backup would put your cycle data on servers, creating exactly the kind of central copy we're trying to avoid. So Cycle Easy keeps it out of iCloud and computer backups too. Export to a file when you want a copy you control.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Is this a medical device?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>No. Cycle Easy is a personal tracking tool, not a medical device. It should not be used for medical diagnosis, treatment decisions, or contraception. Always consult healthcare providers for medical concerns.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>

        </div>

        <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-[var(--border-color)]">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-4">Still need help?</h2>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Email us at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Cycle%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a>. We typically respond within 24-48 hours.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>

<style>
  .faq-section {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .faq-category {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-primary, #e11d48);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color, #e5e5e5);
    padding: 1rem 0;
  }

  .faq-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .faq-question {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary, #0a0a0a);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .faq-question::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-question::after {
    content: '+';
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary, #737373);
    transition: transform 0.2s;
  }

  details[open] .faq-question::after {
    content: '−';
  }

  .faq-answer {
    padding-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary, #737373);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .faq-answer p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .faq-answer p + p {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .faq-answer strong {
    color: var(--text-primary, #0a0a0a);
  }

  :global(.dark) .faq-question {
    color: var(--text-primary, #fafafa);
  }

  :global(.dark) .faq-answer strong {
    color: var(--text-primary, #fafafa);
  }
</style>
